<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jaja of Opobo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1821–<a href="/years/1891">1891</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as King Jaja</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jaja of Opobo was a merchant king in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-delta">Niger Delta</a>. Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igboland">Igboland</a> and sold as a boy into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> in Bonny, he rose to head the Anna Pepple trading house and in 1869 founded the Kingdom of Opobo, which took control of much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palm-oil">palm oil</a> trade. He resisted British commercial control until the consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harry-johnston">Harry Johnston</a> deported him in 1887; he died in 1891 while returning from exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jaja-of-opobo.jpg" alt="Jaja of Opobo" width="320" height="571" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jaja_of_Opobo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
